WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.299 --> 00:00:16.789
Four years ago I uploaded a video explaining
how Littlefinger might have caused Robert's

00:00:16.789 --> 00:00:20.710
Rebellion,
it was well received and well liked theory.

00:00:20.710 --> 00:00:25.559
Now that House of the Dragon is coming in
just over a year, that theory (if true) might

00:00:25.559 --> 00:00:30.529
be more significant than ever before.
House of the Dragon is a Game of Thrones prequel

00:00:30.529 --> 00:00:34.770
show that is confirmed by HBO’s president
to air in 2022.

00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:40.210
Miguel Sapochnik and Ryan Condal will serve
as showrunners and executive producers. George

00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:42.829
R. R. Martin will also serve as executive
producer.

00:00:42.829 --> 00:00:49.280
It is based on George RR Martin’s book Fire
And Blood volume 1 and on Martin’s yet unfinished

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:52.930
Fire And Blood volume 2 book.
“Fire &amp; Blood begins their tale with the

00:00:52.930 --> 00:00:57.790
legendary Aegon the Conqueror, creator of
the Iron Throne, and goes on to recount the

00:00:57.790 --> 00:01:02.539
generations of Targaryens who fought to hold
that iconic seat, all the way up to the civil

00:01:02.539 --> 00:01:07.420
war that nearly tore their dynasty apart.”
In other words it covers events from Aegon's

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:11.850
Conquest to the Dance of the Dragons.
Thats Fire And Blood volume 1.

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:15.950
House of the Dragon will start with a build
up towards the Dance of the Dragons and early

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:21.110
seasons will cover the Dance itself. Later
seasons however, will be based on George RR

00:01:21.110 --> 00:01:24.250
Martin’s yet unfinished Fire And Blood volume
2 book .

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:29.650
The yet unreleased Fire And Blood volume 2
will continue from where part 1 ended, with

00:01:29.650 --> 00:01:35.310
Rhaenyra Targaryen's son Aegon lll's reign
and will cover Blackyre rebellions, war with

00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:40.830
Dorne and go all the way to the Mad King and
Robert's Rebellion that ended Targaryen dynasty.

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:44.869
In this video I'm going to tell you a theory
of mine that I came up with 4 years ago

00:01:44.869 --> 00:01:49.450
in which Littlefinger caused Robert's Rebellion
and ultimately the end of the Targaryens.

00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:54.640
Since the first season of Game of Thrones
we have learned that Petyr Baelish is a cunning,

00:01:54.640 --> 00:02:00.360
unpredictable and ruthless manipulator of
court politcs. As Varys observed himself,

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:05.099
Littlefinger is a grasper from a minor House
with great skill at befriending and eventually

00:02:05.099 --> 00:02:09.370
maneuvering powerful people.
His treatment by the Tullys when he was a

00:02:09.370 --> 00:02:14.310
young man, and his near death at the hand
of Brandon Stark, embittered him against both,

00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:19.680
the Tullys and the Starks. Littlefinger had
orchestrated the entire War of the Five Kings,

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:24.780
the war in which tens of thousands of soldiers
and civilians died. Littlefinger`s, we can

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:30.430
call it genius plan back in season 1, was
to kill Jon Arryn with the help of Jon`s own

00:02:30.430 --> 00:02:33.670
wife, which he did,
and then to make Ned Stark as the new hand

00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:39.640
of the king, whereupon he helped Ned to figure
out who Joffrey`s real father was. Littlefinger

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:44.470
knew that it would lead honorable Ned to reveal
the truth to everyone else, which led to King

00:02:44.470 --> 00:02:49.210
Robert Baratheon`s death as well as to Ned
Stark`s beheading , which started the War

00:02:49.210 --> 00:02:54.070
of the Five Kings. Littlefinger also made
it seem like Lannisters tried to kill Bran

00:02:54.070 --> 00:02:58.690
when in fact it was his doing. Long story
short, Littlefinger threw the Seven Kingdoms

00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:04.510
into the state of chaos from which he personally
benefited. Let me highlight one Varys`s qoute

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:10.489
regarding Littlefinger - ``Littlefinger was
born with no lands, no wealth, no armies.

00:03:10.489 --> 00:03:15.959
He's acquired the first two. How long before
he has the army? Perhaps you`ll laugh, but

00:03:15.959 --> 00:03:20.710
I know him better than most, and this is the
truth. Littlefinger is one of the most dangerous

00:03:20.710 --> 00:03:25.360
men in Westeros.``And let me also say that
this conversation between Varys and Olenna

00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:30.330
took place in the fourth episode of the third
season. Meanwhile Littlefinger married Lysa

00:03:30.330 --> 00:03:35.950
Tully, widow of Lord Jon Arryn of the Vale
who poisoned Jon on Littlefinger`s order,

00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:41.000
and therefore Petyr Baelish became the Lord
Protector of the Vale. As Varys said, Littlefinger

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:46.250
became very powerful man with lands and wealth,
and even managed to provide himself an army

00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:51.920
that he's basically commanding, which he made
possible by influencing the young lord Robin,

00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:56.740
the new Lord Paramount of the Vale. Petyr
Baelish also did all he could to set Sansa

00:03:56.740 --> 00:04:00.640
as a Queen in the North.
He betrayed Ned Stark in order to set up a

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:05.880
fight between "wolfs" and "lions", poisoned
Jofrrey at Joffrey`s own wedding with the

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:12.069
help of Olenna Tyrell to "save" Sansa and
then handed her over to Boltons. All in order

00:04:12.069 --> 00:04:16.169
to turn the North against the Boltons, and
to give him an opportunity to lead the knights

00:04:16.169 --> 00:04:22.340
of the Vale that he is commanding, by manipulating
young lord Robin, which he provided by killing

00:04:22.340 --> 00:04:26.960
Robin`s father and mother. All of this was
in order to set Sansa as the Queen in the

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:32.110
North, convinced that it would lead to marriage
between him and the new Queen of the North,

00:04:32.110 --> 00:04:37.060
which would provide him northern army and
thus one step closer to the Iron Throne. As

00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:41.789
we saw in the season 6 finale, in the battle`s
aftermath, Littlefinger approached Sansa in

00:04:41.789 --> 00:04:46.460
the Godswood and admitted that his goal is
to sit on the Iron Throne with her by his

00:04:46.460 --> 00:04:52.389
side, with her as his queen. However, despite
him being arguably the most cunning and the

00:04:52.389 --> 00:04:58.099
most intelligent player in the game, Baelish
is not incapable of making mistakes and his

00:04:58.099 --> 00:05:03.520
plan to manipulate Sansa failed when the all
seeing Bran Stark returned home. With all

00:05:03.520 --> 00:05:08.360
of this being said, let`s see if there's any
evidence that Petyr Baelish, beside orchestrating

00:05:08.360 --> 00:05:13.800
a major civil war in the Seven Kingdoms, known
as the War of the Five Kings, also orchestrated

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:19.409
the great civil war among the Great Houses
of Westeros, known as the War of the Usurper

00:05:19.409 --> 00:05:24.530
or more popularly, Robert`s Rebellion. As
we all know, Robert`s rebellion resulted in

00:05:24.530 --> 00:05:29.110
the collapse of the Targaryen dynasty and
the ascension of Robert Baratheon to the Iron

00:05:29.110 --> 00:05:33.820
Throne. I know that most of you are probably
confused at this point and are probably wondering

00:05:33.820 --> 00:05:39.339
why would have and how could have he orchestrated
Robert`s rebellion. Well, it`s actually pretty

00:05:39.339 --> 00:05:43.840
simple, and there are two reasons, revenge
and benefit, and in the following minutes

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:47.210
you will be introduced with how exactly he
might have done it.

00:05:47.210 --> 00:05:52.680
Petyr`s father served well under Lord Hoster
Tully and through their good relationship

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:58.499
Hoster agreed to foster his son Petyr at Riverrun,
which was a great honor for House Baelish.

00:05:58.499 --> 00:06:03.919
Petyr went to Riverrun when he was eight years
old and there he befriended Hoster`s daughters

00:06:03.919 --> 00:06:09.689
Catelyn and Lysa Tully, while their brother
Edmure mockingly nicknamed him ``Littlefinger``,

00:06:09.689 --> 00:06:14.439
the nickname that would stick with him through
his entire life. Petyr became obsessed with

00:06:14.439 --> 00:06:20.259
Catelyn, but she never returned his affections.
Eventually when she was engaged to Brandon

00:06:20.259 --> 00:06:25.610
Stark, Ned`s older brother, heir to Lord of
Winterfell and Lord Paramount of the North,

00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:31.800
Petyr challenged him to a duel. Brandon defeated
Baelish easily, nearly disemboweling him in

00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:37.409
the process, but Catelyn begged Brandon to
spare his life. The maesters were able to

00:06:37.409 --> 00:06:42.740
save Baelish and he eventually recovered,
but he was left with a deep scar running from

00:06:42.740 --> 00:06:48.490
his stomach to his collarbone, a token from
Brandon that Baelish would carry with him.

00:06:48.490 --> 00:06:54.180
After this, Baelish was cast out of Riverrun
and returned to Vale. Later, Brandon Stark

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:59.529
who had been on his way to Riverrun to wed
Catelyn Tully was enraged due to false information

00:06:59.529 --> 00:07:04.849
about Prince Rhaegar Targaryen`s abduction
over his sister Lyanna, and instead to Riverrun,

00:07:04.849 --> 00:07:10.319
he rode to King`s Landing immediately to demand
Rhaegar`s arrest and punishment. Aerys ``the

00:07:10.319 --> 00:07:15.369
Mad King`` arrested Brandon for treason and
eventually killed him and his father Rickard

00:07:15.369 --> 00:07:21.150
in a horrific and unjust way, which led to
Houses Baratheon, Stark and Arryn rebelling

00:07:21.150 --> 00:07:26.719
against the Iron Throne. Now, in my opinion,
those false rumors about Rhaegar`s abduction

00:07:26.719 --> 00:07:31.399
over Lyanna that basically started Robert`s
Rebellion were started by none other than

00:07:31.399 --> 00:07:36.569
Petyr Baelish himself. As we learned in later
seasons of Game of Thrones, Rhaegar did not

00:07:36.569 --> 00:07:41.930
kidnap Lyanna, but they rather loved each
other and went away together. However it's

00:07:41.930 --> 00:07:47.910
still unknown why they decided to leave without
a word, knowing this could start a war. Knowing

00:07:47.910 --> 00:07:53.539
how kind and noble Rhaegar and Lyanna were,
it`s also hard to believe they would let the

00:07:53.539 --> 00:07:58.629
Seven Kingdoms as well as their own families
burn for their love. On the one hand we have

00:07:58.629 --> 00:08:03.050
Brandon who at a time had been on his way
to Riverrun to wed Catelyn Tully, while on

00:08:03.050 --> 00:08:07.180
the other hand we have Lyanna who was in the
Riverlands when she departed with Rhaegar

00:08:07.180 --> 00:08:11.560
to the Tower of Joy. When you take a close
look, it does seem possible that Littlefinger

00:08:11.560 --> 00:08:16.369
spread the false rumors of Rhaegar abducting
Lyanna in order to prevent a wedding between

00:08:16.369 --> 00:08:21.469
his beloved Catelyn and Brandon Stark as well
as to seek revenge against Brandon who almost

00:08:21.469 --> 00:08:26.090
killed him sometime earlier. Now before I
go any further, let me just show you one clip

00:08:26.090 --> 00:08:57.690
from the third episode of the very first season
that's going in favor to this theory.

00:08:57.690 --> 00:09:02.661
As we can see, Eddard was furious when Littlefinger
brought him to a brothel, believing that he

00:09:02.661 --> 00:09:08.380
is a victim of a bad joke, but Catelyn intervened
when Ned attacked Littlefinger,

00:09:08.380 --> 00:09:12.680
whereupon Littlefinger said ``the Starks..
quick tempers, slow minds``.

00:09:12.680 --> 00:09:16.839
Could it be that Littlefinger spread false
rumors about Rhaegar`s abduction over Lyanna

00:09:16.839 --> 00:09:22.209
Stark knowing that it would lead quick tempered
Brandon Stark who was also known as the wild

00:09:22.209 --> 00:09:25.250
wolf
to do something honorable and stupid at the

00:09:25.250 --> 00:09:30.110
same time, which would result with Brandon
not continuing his travel to Riverrun to wed

00:09:30.110 --> 00:09:35.839
Catelyn, but instead to ride to King`s Landing
and eventually die, which is exactly what

00:09:35.839 --> 00:09:40.279
happened. Could it be that this Littlefinger`s
quote about the Starks was actually a foreshadow

00:09:40.279 --> 00:09:45.580
of Ned Stark`s death, because just as Brandon,
Ned Stark had a quick temper,

00:09:45.580 --> 00:09:50.660
but slow mind to figure out Littlefinger`s
manipulation. In the seventh episode of the

00:09:50.660 --> 00:09:56.250
first season, Littlefinger said there's one
thing he learned from losing his duel to Brandon

00:09:56.250 --> 00:09:59.449
Stark,
he learned that he will never win on their,

00:09:59.449 --> 00:10:05.029
honorable way,but will rather as he said himself
- manipulate them to provide himself everything

00:10:05.029 --> 00:10:10.240
he wants, which at first was Catelyn Tully
and revenge against Brandon Stark. There is

00:10:10.240 --> 00:10:15.290
a high possibility that Littlefinger did spread
false rumours about Rhaegar`s kidnap over

00:10:15.290 --> 00:10:20.540
Lyanna in order to prevent Brandon Stark`s
marriage with his beloved Catelyn,

00:10:20.540 --> 00:10:25.519
since he knew Brandon had a quick temper,which
instead of thinking twice about his next act

00:10:25.519 --> 00:10:30.290
resulted with him riding to King`s Landing
immediately and demanding justice from the

00:10:30.290 --> 00:10:33.699
Mad King,
which resulted just as Littlefinger wanted,

00:10:33.699 --> 00:10:38.769
with Brandon’s death. There's one more fact
that is going in favor to this theory, which

00:10:38.769 --> 00:10:44.121
is confirmation of Petyr Baelish knowing that
Rhaegar did not abduct Lyanna, which the forth

00:10:44.121 --> 00:10:47.750
episode of the fifth season almost certainly
confirmed.

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:52.310
There's a scene in which Petyr finds Sansa
in the crypts of Winterfell paying her respects

00:10:52.310 --> 00:10:58.450
to her deceased family members. Petyr recalls
about how Rhaegar Targaryen chose Sansa's

00:10:58.450 --> 00:11:03.199
aunt, Lyanna, which started Robert’s rebellion
against the Targaryen family,

00:11:03.199 --> 00:11:07.829
on which Sansa replied with confirming that
Rhaegar did choose her aunt, but against her

00:11:07.829 --> 00:11:10.730
will,
on which Littlefinger didn’t reply, but

00:11:10.730 --> 00:11:14.800
he didn’t even have to, his face expression
was more than enough.

00:11:14.800 --> 00:11:37.709
Littlefinger had known the truth. How did
Littlefinger know the truth in the first place

00:11:37.709 --> 00:11:42.550
to be able to twist it around and spread false
information you might wonder - well, there

00:11:42.550 --> 00:11:47.279
are many possibilities.
Littlefinger like Varys is known to have spies

00:11:47.279 --> 00:11:51.589
everywhere, so that's one possibility.
The other possibility is that he himself saw

00:11:51.589 --> 00:11:55.190
them run away.
The third, more complicated possibility is

00:11:55.190 --> 00:12:00.819
that Littfinger intercepted Lyanna's message
or letter that was meant for her brother Brandon

00:12:00.819 --> 00:12:05.870
in which she wrote that she and Rhaegar are
in love and will spend some time together,

00:12:05.870 --> 00:12:11.339
making sure no bad assumptions arise to start
a war, but Littlfinger simply burned the letter

00:12:11.339 --> 00:12:16.810
and spread the false rumor. I’m convinced
that Littlefinger spread the false rumours

00:12:16.810 --> 00:12:22.089
about Rhaegar’s abduction over Lyanna to
prevent Brandon from marrying his beloved

00:12:22.089 --> 00:12:26.970
Catelyn and to get Brandon killed,
while also starting a civil war from which

00:12:26.970 --> 00:12:31.350
he would benefit as after the war he joins
the small council.

00:12:31.350 --> 00:12:37.480
He did always say that chaos benefits him.
House of the Dragon airs in 2022 and since

00:12:37.480 --> 00:12:42.569
the later seasons will cover Robert's Rebellion,
I’m looking forward to find out why Lyanna

00:12:42.569 --> 00:12:47.040
had not left a simple note for her family
that could have prevented the death of her

00:12:47.040 --> 00:12:51.769
father and brother as well as the deaths of
thousands of soldiers and innocent people

00:12:51.769 --> 00:12:57.180
that died during Robert’s Rebellion. There's
a possibility that Lyanna wrote a note,

00:12:57.180 --> 00:13:02.310
but it was simply handed over to the wrong
person and was never read by the Starks.

00:13:02.310 --> 00:13:06.560
I'm convinced Littlefinger caused Robert's
Rebellion for revenge and benefit.

00:13:06.560 --> 00:13:09.470
Thank you so much for watching, hope you enjoyed
this video and if you did make sure to give

00:13:09.470 --> 00:13:17.500
it a big thumbs up and I hope to see you in
the next one, peace!

